    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2). The implementation is complete. Here's what I changed and why each piece lives where it does:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Contract (`openapi.yml` \u2192 generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`)**\n- Added `addressLine1` and optional `addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema (both `maxLength: 255`). They're inherited by the `Owner` response schema via its existing `allOf`, so they round-trip out automatically.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list so a structured-only request is accepted. `city` stays required. This keeps earlier minimal (flat) owners valid.\n\n**Normalization + composition (single responsibility, reused)**\n- `OwnerAddress.compose(line1, line2)` \u2014 new reusable method: normalizes each line and joins them with a single space, appending line 2 only when it's non-blank. Sits next to the existing `normalize`, keeping the canonical-address rules in one class.\n- `NormalizeOwnerAddress` \u2014 now normalizes whichever address fields are supplied, and **prefers the structured form**: when `addressLine1` is present it sets the flat `address` to the composed lines; otherwise it normalizes the supplied flat `address` in place. Because the effective address lands in the single `address` field, everything downstream that reads it (and the household hash / postcode / locality, which read the shared `city`/`postcode`) sees structured-when-present, flat-otherwise.\n\n**Validation** \u2014 unchanged. Since composition runs *before* `ValidateOwnerFields`, its existing \"`address` + `city` non-blank\" check now means exactly \"non-blank `addressLine1` OR flat `address`, plus city\", with no new branching.\n\n**Persistence & mapping**\n- `Owner` entity: added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` columns + accessors. MapStruct maps them by name in both directions \u2014 no mapper edits needed.\n- Added `address_line1`/`address_line2` columns to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb is what the tests use; the rest for consistency).\n\n**PUT path (consistency)** \u2014 inserted the shared `NormalizeOwnerAddress` step before validation in `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` and updated `ApplyOwner` to copy the structured lines, so updates accept structured addresses the same way creates do \u2014 reusing the same function class rather than duplicating logic.",
